WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:07.173
“It began Saturday morning with 
a massive rocket barrage

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.759
from Gaza striking across Israel.”

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:13.054
In the early hours of Saturday, October 7th...

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.140
Israelis in the south of the country...

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.475
huddled in basements and bomb shelters.

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:19.894
They listened as Hamas militants

00:00:19.894 --> 00:00:21.771
went house to house in their neighborhoods...

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:26.151
brutally killing civilians of all ages 
and taking hostages.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:27.861
These homes were in communities

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:30.530
just a few miles from this border 
with Gaza...

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.407
where for two decades

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.868
the Israeli army has guarded this wall...

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.954
which holds more than 2 million Palestinians

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:40.123
in what's been called 
an open-air prison.

00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:41.541
Little water.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.751
Little electricity.

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.836
Virtually no way out.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:46.546
Hiding in fear.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.757
Israelis texted their 
friends and family

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.550
a very similar question.

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.761
Where is the army?

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:58.308
Israel is one of the biggest military spenders 
in proportion to its population.

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:01.644
That coupled with billions in military aid 
from the US

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:03.605
has made the Israeli military

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.565
one of the most advanced in the world.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.901
We have planes. We have helicopters.
We have tanks.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:08.985
We have everything. 

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:13.114
For the first couple of hours, it's like we have no army.

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:14.699
“The words of survivors...”

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:16.284
“Where was the army?”

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:17.744
“Where was the army?”

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:19.913
You can see the strength of Israel's military

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.915
in its response to the Hamas attacks.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.751
Persistent bombing in Gaza, 
leveling neighborhoods

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.588
killing more than 2000 people,
including at least 700 children.

00:01:28.838 --> 00:01:30.673
Preparing for a ground invasion.

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:33.635
But on the day of the Hamas attacks 
in Israel.

00:01:33.843 --> 00:01:36.096
At the sites of some of the worst violence...

00:01:36.638 --> 00:01:39.015
soldiers didn't arrive for about 8 hours.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:43.144
By then, hundreds were dead, 
missing, or kidnaped.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.814
Why did it take so long?

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:49.150
To answer that question,
we need to look here:

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.401
In the West Bank.

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:56.449
In 1947, this entire area

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.952
was home to nearly 2 million people.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:03.164
The vast majority of them Palestinian Muslims 
and Christians.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.876
When World War II ended in the wake of 
the Holocaust in Europe...

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.420
the newly formed United Nations voted

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.840
to divide this land into two states:

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:13.925
A Jewish state and an Arab state...

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:17.679
with Jerusalem as a separate 
UN-controlled entity.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:21.808
But in 1948 zionist militias and paramilitary groups 
carried out

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.185
a mass expulsion and massacre of Palestinians...

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:27.021
seizing their villages to expand 
the Jewish state.

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:30.942
Then, in 1967, after a war 
with its Arab neighbors...

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.612
Israel occupied the West Bank, East Jerusalem,
and the Gaza Strip

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:37.574
taking more land designated for Palestinians.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.410
And started turning parts of those 
Palestinian territories

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.829
into illegal settlements for Jewish Israelis.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.415
Today, the most extensive examples of that 

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.041
can be found here: 
In the West Bank...

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.335
where some of the settlements 
have gotten so big

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.837
they've achieved city status.

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:53.214
And they're just some of the hundreds of settlements

00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:55.717
in the occupied West Bank 
that have been built on land

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:58.011
originally intended for a Palestinian state.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.180
And where Palestinians still live...

00:03:00.471 --> 00:03:02.056
under Israeli military rule...

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:04.642
with far fewer rights than their Israeli neighbors.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.687
From the very earliest beginnings

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.814
of Netanyahu's career in politics

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:11.399
he's been an opponent 
of the two state solution...

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.193
been in the central part of his ideology.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.904
And it is just intimately bound up 
in his idea

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:17.197
of what Israel is.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.240
That it needs to have control 
of the West Bank.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.869
“Israel must retain the overriding 
security control

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.079
over the entire area west 
of the Jordan River.”

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.124
The government has encouraged 
settlements in the West Bank

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:29.834
like the one advertised here.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:30.877
“Home of your dreams.”

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:34.130
“The tranquility of a picturesque
setting and crisp mountain air...

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:37.175
with all the benefits and amenities
that Jerusalem has to offer.”

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.928
Enormous resources

00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:42.680
have been devoted to this project.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:47.060
And this is bipartisan to put it 
in American terms.

00:03:47.101 --> 00:03:48.853
This is a state project.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:50.605
They are funding them.

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:51.940
They're paving roads for them.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.858
They're providing security for them.

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:55.526
They're creating infrastructure

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:57.403
and water and electricity for them.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:00.365
Tax breaks to incentivize Israelis to move there.

00:04:01.115 --> 00:04:03.743
The number of Israeli Jewish settlers
in the West Bank

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:07.497
began growing before Netanyahu 
came to power in 1996...

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:11.793
and continued even when he was 
out of office from 2000 to 2009.

00:04:12.126 --> 00:04:15.630
But if you look at the number of 
new settlement outposts each year...

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.174
you can see that there's 
a noticeable gap right here.

00:04:18.174 --> 00:04:19.592
Under international pressure...

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:21.427
those new outposts were halted.

00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:23.930
But after Netanyahu came back to power...

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:27.267
his government started legalizing
some of those old settlements.

00:04:27.642 --> 00:04:30.395
And at the same time, they built
and promoted new ones.

00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:33.773
As this map shows, they've proliferated 
ever since.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:38.695
This is a project of slow-motion colonization.

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:40.613
So what you have is Palestinians

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.032
living in these tiny little pockets

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:45.451
these little urban islands of control.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.954
And so when you look at the West Bank...

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:51.958
what you see is that more than 60% of it

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.919
is under full Israeli control 
and administration.

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:58.881
And that's where the more sparsely populated 
Palestinian communities are

00:04:58.881 --> 00:05:02.176
that are slowly being forcibly transferred.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.805
The United Nations put out a report...

00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:09.017
saying that since the beginning of 2022...

00:05:09.183 --> 00:05:13.021
more than 1,100 Palestinian Bedouins

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:17.275
have been forcibly transferred from 
their communities in the West Bank.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:22.030
In the founding statute of 
the International Criminal Court

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.449
there is a section defining war crimes.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:27.160
The transfer, directly or indirectly

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.456
by the occupying power of parts of 
its own civilian population 

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:33.666
into the territory it occupies.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:38.838
Or the deportation or transfer of all 
or parts of the population

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:42.842
of the occupied territory 
within or outside this territory.

00:05:43.051 --> 00:05:45.345
It's part of the reason why the United Nations

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.180
has called the Israeli settlements...

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.599
unlawful under international law.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.185
But Salem, a Jerusalem-based nonprofit...

00:05:52.226 --> 00:05:54.771
has documented numerous instances 
of violence

00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:56.689
against Palestinians in the West Bank.

00:05:57.357 --> 00:06:00.860
Israeli settlers have attacked 
Palestinian houses with stones...

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:02.028
torched cars...

00:06:02.278 --> 00:06:04.906
vandalized a supermarket 
and burned homes.

00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:06.866
According to other reports

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:10.119
the Israeli military has killed 
hundreds of Palestinians

00:06:10.119 --> 00:06:13.039
in a series of violent events
this year alone.

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:24.217
The deal with Israelis is, we will live 
in these dangerous places...

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.887
and you, the army, will protect us.

00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:30.890
So at that point settlement enterprise necessitates

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.642
the misallocation of military resources.

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:36.312
Those were the military resources 
that were missing

00:06:36.312 --> 00:06:39.232
when Hamas broke through 
the border with Gaza.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.734
There were empty posts 
on the border there.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:44.862
Troops weren't getting the proper 
security notifications.

00:06:44.987 --> 00:06:47.532
It was clear that the entire system...

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.742
for monitoring...

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.702
what was happening on the Gaza border
had broken down.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.580
There is a real ground swell

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.501
among the Israeli population that 
this was just an immense disaster

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.086
presided over by Netanyahu.

00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:02.463
And in the West Bank, 
trying to colonize it

00:07:02.463 --> 00:07:04.173
and seize Palestinian lands...

00:07:04.215 --> 00:07:07.385
that you devoted resources and attention 
to those initiatives...

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:11.681
at the expense of protecting us
from Hamas.

00:07:17.352 --> 00:07:19.354
“We have to go immediately.”

00:07:19.597 --> 00:07:20.473
“Immediately.”

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:21.766
“He is a murderer.”

00:07:21.766 --> 00:07:25.478
“We’re all very, very frustrated 
that he's still there.”

00:07:26.036 --> 00:07:28.998
A recent poll found that four out of five
Jewish Israelis

00:07:28.998 --> 00:07:33.586
believe the government and Prime Minister Netanyahu 
are to blame for the attacks.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:37.030
More than half say he should resign 
when the war is over.

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:42.378
Netanyahu really has been
the architect

00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:44.297
of Israel's long term strategy towards Gaza.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.840
That's happened under his administration.

00:07:46.207 --> 00:07:47.959
He thought that he could contain Hamas

00:07:47.959 --> 00:07:49.002
deter it from doing the worst stuff.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.536
Periodically fight with them in ways

00:07:51.536 --> 00:07:53.788
that would not hurt very many 
Israeli civilians...

00:07:53.972 --> 00:07:57.251
and encourage division between 
Hamas and the West Bank...

00:07:57.251 --> 00:07:59.587
to make sure that the Palestinians 
could not make

00:07:59.587 --> 00:08:01.172
a more credible case for a peace agreement.

00:08:01.268 --> 00:08:02.811
That policy has just...

00:08:02.811 --> 00:08:04.480
it's an obvious failure at this point.

